# Shared engineering rules

* Work in small, reviewable increments.
* Prefer Babashka for scripts where it fits the project.
* Prefer the project's established unit-test style; Speclj is a suitable
  default for Clojure-family projects when no local standard exists.
* Keep pure `.cljc` code independent of desktop, browser, filesystem, audio,
  and network details.
* Separate testable code from GUI/device/environment boundaries.
* Keep property testing separate from ordinary unit verification.
* Use APS tools for Gherkin parsing and mutation rather than reimplementing the
  parser.
* Do not hand-edit mutation manifests or generated acceptance output.
* Run verification sequentially when generation and execution share artifacts.
